Inkshift — The Sky Fractures: credits

Picture
- Everything on screen is drawn by the code in this folder (three.js scenes, custom shaders, Canvas 2D). No images, models,
  textures, fonts or video are loaded. The reference image used while designing the style was not used in any frame.
- three.js r170 (MIT) — https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js
- Lemo-Opuscar core render tools and core/lib.js helpers (MIT, see LICENSE at the repository root).

Sound (ElevenLabs sound effects, eleven_text_to_sound_v2, generated on the author's account; files in demo/audio/, not in git)
- amb_city (9 s, loop, influence 0.45): Night on a high city rooftop: distant traffic hum far below, soft steady wind across
  the roof, one faint far-off siren, no voices, calm and wide
- crack_tick (1.5 s, 0.6): A thin bright crackle high in the sky, like a sheet of paper and thin glass beginning to split far
  away, delicate, with a faint shimmering ring
- crack_run (1.2 s, 0.55): A fast crackling split racing downward, dry paper and thin ice tearing, sizzling and rising in
  pitch, ending abruptly
- fracture (3 s, 0.5): One violent rip of a huge sheet of thick paper, layered with a deep sub-bass boom and a sharp
  controlled impact, then a low tonal swell that bends slowly downward, cinematic
- rise (4.5 s, 0.45): Massive buildings slowly lifting off the ground into the sky: deep groaning rumble, creaking steel,
  crumbling concrete, reversed debris whooshes drifting upward, dreamlike and cinematic
- echo (1.8 s, 0.55): A short reversed swell into a soft slightly detuned glassy chime with a spacious slapback echo,
  ethereal, fragments drifting left and right
- reveal (2.2 s, 0.5): A low cinematic orchestral swell of warm brass and low strings that shifts from a dark minor chord to
  a bright open chord, short and resonant
- drone (8.5 s, 0.45): Deep cinematic tension drone, low strings and a soft analog synth pad, slowly rising and mysterious,
  no percussion
- reach (1 s, 0.55): A heavy wool coat sleeve rustling as an arm lifts quickly, with a small sharp intake of breath
